.SS " Optional[\fBTag\fP] bs4\&.BeautifulSoup\&.handle_starttag ( self, str name, Optional[str] namespace, Optional[str] nsprefix, _RawAttributeValues attrs, Optional[int]  sourceline = \fCNone\fP, Optional[int]  sourcepos = \fCNone\fP, Optional[Dict[str, str]]  namespaces = \fCNone\fP)"

.PP
.nf
Called by the tree builder when a new tag is encountered\&.

:param name: Name of the tag\&.
:param nsprefix: Namespace prefix for the tag\&.
:param attrs: A dictionary of attribute values\&. Note that
   attribute values are expected to be simple strings; processing
   of multi-valued attributes such as 'class' comes later\&.
:param sourceline: The line number where this tag was found in its
    source document\&.
:param sourcepos: The character position within `sourceline` where this
    tag was found\&.
:param namespaces: A dictionary of all namespace prefix mappings
    currently in scope in the document\&.

If this method returns None, the tag was rejected by an active
`ElementFilter`\&. You should proceed as if the tag had not occurred
in the document\&. For instance, if this was a self-closing tag,
don't call handle_endtag\&.

:meta private:

.fi
